      "en": "DOCTEUR RÉVILLE (Scene 18, turn 175): The pride of virtue is often more wounding to a proud spirit than direct vengeance. We measure there the mystery of redemptive grace that shatters moral pride and transfigures suffering into spiritual intersubjectivity."
